<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Maple Grove &mdash; Full Deep-Dive</title><style>body{font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:#1a1a1a;line-height:1.5;}h1{font-size:16pt;color:#1e3a5f;border-bottom:2pt solid #e8a020;padding-bottom:4pt;margin-bottom:2pt;}h2{font-size:13pt;color:#1e3a5f;margin:14pt 0 4pt;border-bottom:1pt solid #edf0f4;padding-bottom:2pt;}h3{font-size:11.5pt;color:#1e3a5f;margin:11pt 0 3pt;}a{color:#1155cc;text-decoration:underline;}.banner{background:#fff4d6;border:1pt solid #e8a020;color:#7a5b00;font-size:9.5pt;padding:6pt 9pt;margin:0 0 12pt;}.sub{color:#4a5568;font-size:10pt;margin:2pt 0 4pt;}.hdr{font-size:10pt;color:#23344a;margin:1pt 0;}.hdr b{color:#1e3a5f;}.outcome{font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;color:#14532d;background:#e8f5ec;border-left:3pt solid #1a7a4a;padding:6pt 9pt;margin:8pt 0;}.bottomline{background:#eef3fa;border-left:3pt solid #1e3a5f;padding:6pt 9pt;margin:8pt 0;}ul{margin:4pt 0 8pt 0;}li{margin:2pt 0;}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:10pt;margin:6pt 0;}th,td{border:1pt solid #cdd6e0;padding:4pt 6pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;}th{background:#1e3a5f;color:#fff;font-size:9.5pt;}blockquote{margin:5pt 0 5pt 14pt;padding:3pt 0 3pt 10pt;border-left:2pt solid #cdd6e0;color:#33414f;font-style:italic;}.spk{font-style:normal;font-weight:bold;color:#1e3a5f;}.meta{color:#4a5568;font-size:9pt;border-top:1pt solid #edf0f4;padding-top:6pt;margin-top:18pt;}</style></head><body><h1>Maple Grove &mdash; Full Deep-Dive</h1><p class="sub">Detailed segment summary &middot; Version 3 of 3 (Full Deep-Dive)</p><div class="banner"><b>DRAFT — illustrative example.</b> Structure proposal only. Built around a fictional Westfield, IN rezoning hearing to demonstrate the format; figures are not real and are pending validation against the 10-segment research study (see proposal &sect;5). Timestamp links are illustrative.</div><div class="hdr"><b>Project:</b> Maple Grove &mdash; residential PUD subdivision</div><div class="hdr"><b>Jurisdiction / body:</b> City of Westfield, Hamilton County, IN &middot; Advisory Plan Commission</div><div class="hdr"><b>Meeting date:</b> May 19, 2026</div><div class="hdr"><b>Agenda item:</b> Docket 2605-PUD-04 &middot; Ordinance 26-15 (rezone AG-SF1 &rarr; PUD)</div><div class="hdr"><b>Segment:</b> <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1122s">[18:42]</a>&ndash;<a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2490s">[41:30]</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1122s">open video at segment start</a></div><h2>Chronological timestamp index</h2><table><tr><th>Time</th><th>Speaker / role</th><th>Topic</th></tr><tr><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1122s">[18:42]</a></td><td>M. Foss, Planning Director</td><td>Staff report &amp; recommendation</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1215s">[20:15]</a></td><td>B. Reardon, petitioner&rsquo;s attorney</td><td>Project overview</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1420s">[23:40]</a></td><td>P. Nair, engineer</td><td>Concept plan, open space, drainage</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1670s">[27:50]</a></td><td>Commissioners</td><td>Q&amp;A: traffic &amp; schools</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1865s">[31:05]</a></td><td>M. Dunn, Commissioner</td><td>Sequencing of traffic study</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1990s">[33:10]</a></td><td>Public</td><td>Public comment opens</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2285s">[38:05]</a></td><td>Commission</td><td>Condition deliberation</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2420s">[40:20]</a></td><td>L. Park / T. Becker</td><td>Motion &amp; second</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2465s">[41:05]</a></td><td>D. Whitfield, President</td><td>Roll-call vote</td></tr></table><h2>Request</h2><p>Petition of Arbor Homes LLC / Maple Grove Development Partners (Docket <b>2605-PUD-04</b>, Ordinance <b>26-15</b>) to rezone approximately 62.0 acres (Parcel 29-09-..., NE corner 161st St &amp; Oak Rd) from <b>AG-SF1</b> to <b>PUD</b> for 184 detached single-family lots; min lot width 60 ft; min lot area 7,200 sf; ~12.1 ac open space; gross density ~3.0 du/ac. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1215s">[20:15]</a></p><h2>Proceedings</h2><h3>Staff report</h3><p>Planning Director Megan Foss presented the staff analysis and a recommendation of approval with conditions. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1122s">[18:42]</a></p><blockquote><span class="spk">Foss:</span> &ldquo;The proposed density is consistent with the low-density residential designation in the 2023 comprehensive plan. Staff&rsquo;s recommendation is favorable, conditioned on a traffic study and the buffering shown on sheet 4.&rdquo; <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1195s">[19:55]</a></blockquote><h3>Petitioner presentation</h3><blockquote><span class="spk">Reardon:</span> &ldquo;This is attainable move-up product. We are committing to the Monon trail stub and to twelve acres of open space maintained by the HOA, not the City.&rdquo; <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1290s">[21:30]</a></blockquote><blockquote><span class="spk">Nair:</span> &ldquo;Stormwater is handled by two regional ponds; the east buffer preserves the existing tree line.&rdquo; <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1450s">[24:10]</a></blockquote><h3>Commissioner questions &amp; concerns</h3><blockquote><span class="spk">Reynolds:</span> &ldquo;What is the trip count at 161st and Oak at build-out?&rdquo; <span class="spk">Nair:</span> &ldquo;A full study is pending; preliminary counts suggest a left-turn lane may be warranted.&rdquo; <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1700s">[28:20]</a></blockquote><blockquote><span class="spk">Dunn:</span> &ldquo;I&rsquo;m uncomfortable recommending approval before we see the traffic study, not after.&rdquo; <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1865s">[31:05]</a></blockquote><h3>Public comment</h3><table><tr><th>Speaker</th><th>Position</th><th>Key point</th><th>Time</th></tr><tr><td>Karen Mills</td><td>Against</td><td>Cut-through traffic on Oak Rd</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2005s">[33:25]</a></td></tr><tr><td>David Cho</td><td>Against</td><td>Elementary school at capacity</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2110s">[35:10]</a></td></tr><tr><td>Susan Albright</td><td>For</td><td>Local shortage of attainable housing</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2200s">[36:40]</a></td></tr></table><h2>Conditions &amp; commitments (verbatim)</h2><ul><li>&ldquo;A traffic impact study shall be completed and submitted prior to the City Council hearing, with improvements at 161st &amp; Oak Rd as warranted.&rdquo; <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2300s">[38:20]</a></li><li>&ldquo;A minimum twenty-foot tree-preservation buffer shall be maintained along the east property line.&rdquo; <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2335s">[38:55]</a></li><li>&ldquo;The developer shall construct a pedestrian connection to the planned Monon extension.&rdquo; <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2370s">[39:30]</a></li><li>&ldquo;No less than twelve acres of open space, maintained by the HOA.&rdquo; <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2390s">[39:50]</a></li></ul><h2>Procedural notes</h2><ul><li>No continuance; petition heard and acted on the same night. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2285s">[38:05]</a></li><li>No recusals declared.</li><li>Motion amended once to add the trail-connection condition before the vote. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2405s">[40:05]</a></li></ul><h2>Motion &amp; roll-call vote</h2><p>Moved by Park, seconded by Becker: forward to Council with a favorable recommendation subject to the four conditions. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2420s">[40:20]</a></p><table><tr><th>Member</th><th>Vote</th></tr><tr><td>Dana Whitfield (President)</td><td>Aye</td></tr><tr><td>Raymond Ortiz (Vice President)</td><td>Aye</td></tr><tr><td>Lena Park</td><td>Aye</td></tr><tr><td>Tom Becker</td><td>Aye</td></tr><tr><td>Aisha Reynolds</td><td>Aye</td></tr><tr><td>Greg Halloran</td><td>Aye</td></tr><tr><td>Marcus Dunn</td><td>Nay</td></tr></table><p><b>Result: 6&ndash;1, favorable recommendation.</b> <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2465s">[41:05]</a></p><h2>Outcome &amp; next steps</h2><p>Forwarded to Westfield City Council (tentative June 8, 2026) for action on Ordinance 26-15. Final rezone requires Council adoption. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2490s">[41:30]</a></p><h2>Appendix</h2><ul><li><b>Agenda item text:</b> &ldquo;Docket 2605-PUD-04 &mdash; Maple Grove PUD, rezone ~62 ac AG-SF1 to PUD, 184 lots.&rdquo;</li><li><b>Ordinance reference:</b> 26-15.</li><li><b>Related prior hearings:</b> Technical Advisory Committee review (Apr 30, 2026); concept pre-application (Mar 2026).</li></ul><p class="meta"><b>Sources:</b> <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519">Meeting recording (YouTube)</a> &middot; <a href="#">Agenda packet (PDF)</a> &middot; <a href="#">Staff report (PDF)</a><br>Detailed agenda-item summary &mdash; generated from the meeting transcript by MRD (Municipal Resource Dashboard), scoped to this project&rsquo;s agenda item. Timestamp links open the cited moment in the source video.</p></body></html>